 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S446-005\", \"clauses\": {\"add\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} + {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F16 is a question_text family whose two slots take numbers from the generated values a and b; it is the direct addition question.\"}, \"numbers\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} + {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F16 presents two numbers to be added, drawn from a and b, which have printed runs from the low thousands to 9997 in a problem.\"}, \"sums_up_to_10000\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} + {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The declared max_sum bound is 10000 and F16 prints a and b whose observed runs reach 9992 and 8480; sums in the observed result runs of F09 reach 9999, so sums up to 10 000 are produced.\"}, \"with_regrouping\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} + {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The declared regrouping variants one_place, two_places, three_places and four_places select regrouping problems, and F16 renders those addends as the question.\"}, \"without_regrouping\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} + {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The declared regrouping variant none selects problems with no carry, and F16 renders those addends as the question.\"}, \"regrouping\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is {a} + {b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The task of regrouping is performed by answering F16 with a regrouping variant; the hint family F06 names the regroup step but is not a problem family.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F08\", \"F09\", \"F10\", \"F11\", \"F12\", \"F14\", \"F15\", \"F16\", \"F17\", \"F18\", \"F19\", \"F20\", \"F21\", \"F22\", \"F25\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"We are adding two numbers: {a} and {b}.\", \"{capitalize} is {a} + {b} = {result}.\", \"Start at {a}. Count up {b} more. You land on ___\", \"{a} + {b} = ___\", \"Start at {slot}. Count up {slot2} more. You land on {slot3}\", \"{actor} solved: \\\"{problem}\\\". {actor} says the {miss} is {answer}. Is {actor} correct?\", \"{slot} + {slot2} = {slot3}\", \"What is {a} + {b}?\", \"Start at {a}. Count up {b} more. You land on {fill_value}.\", \"{a} + {b} = {fill_value}\", \"{statement}. True or False?\", \"The two parts are {p1} and {p2}. What is the {word}?\", \"Show {a} + {b} on the number line.\", \"The dot is at {a} and it moves forward {b} {num_word}. Starting from {a}, just count up {b} {num_word}. Which number will the dot land on?\", \"{prefix}What is {a} + {b}?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"The vocabulary block declares number_format as the space separator for thousands, with the example written in the file, and the competency text itself writes the bound with that separator. The observed printed_runs of every family that prints a four-digit number show the values unseparated: for example, the a-run of F08 includes 1040 and 1081, and the result-run of F09 includes 1030 and 1330, with no separator anywhere in the observed renders. F08, F09, F10, F11, F12, F14, F15, F16, F17, F18, F20, F21, F22 and F25 print these values directly, and F19 prints them through its nested statement families F17 and F18. Each failing template is the question or statement the learner reads, and the wrong format sits in every render of it. This is a format fault against the lc's declared ground truth, not an arithmetic or vocabulary fault; the vocabulary gate is correct (F01 prints regroup for regrouping; F02 and F20 print sum; F14 prints missing number, which is cumulative), and no NOT_YET_KNOWN term appears in any family's text. F22 also frames counting up by b numbers with b up to 8831, which a learner cannot count; I note it as a load concern but do not fail it separately because F10 and F17 use the same counting-up spine within the lc's scope. F21 asks the learner to show a sum on a number line with no keyed answer slot; the owner ruling that a draw is an interactive visual covers it, so it is not separately failed. The clause verdicts above are all PRODUCIBLE by F16, the family that renders the addition question under each declared regrouping variant.\"}",
